1. App Vision & Overview
App Name: TechPulse (working title — agents can suggest alternatives)
One-liner: A cross-platform mobile app that auto-curates the week’s most relevant tech topics based on a user’s selected technology stack, then generates an infographic-style newsletter and personalized learning plan every week.
Target Platforms: iOS & Android (single codebase via Kotlin Multiplatform + Compose Multiplatform)
Core Value Proposition:
•	Eliminates information overload — users don’t manually browse 20+ sources
•	Personalized to their exact tech stack (e.g., "Spring Boot + Kafka + PostgreSQL + Kubernetes")
•	Delivers a visually rich, shareable weekly newsletter — not just a text dump
•	Builds a cumulative learning plan that evolves weekly
 
2. Functional Requirements
2.1 Onboarding & User Profile
Feature	Details
Sign-up/Login	Email + password, Google OAuth, Apple Sign-In (required for iOS App Store). JWT-based auth tokens with refresh mechanism.
Tech Stack Selector	Multi-select UI with categories: Languages (Java, Kotlin, Python, Go, Rust…), Frameworks (Spring Boot, Django, React, Angular…), Cloud (AWS, Azure, GCP…), DevOps (K8s, Docker, Terraform…), Data (PostgreSQL, Kafka, Redis…), AI/ML (LLMs, PyTorch, MLOps…). Allow custom tags.
Interest Level	Per-topic: Beginner / Intermediate / Advanced — drives learning plan depth
Notification Preferences	Day/time for weekly delivery, push notification toggle
Profile Management	Edit tech stack, change delivery day, manage notification preferences

2.2 Weekly Content Aggregation (Backend)
Feature	Details
Automated Cron Job	Runs every Sunday midnight UTC (configurable). Uses Spring Scheduler or Quartz.
Source Aggregation	Pull from: Hacker News API, Dev.to API, Reddit API (subreddits per tech), GitHub Trending, RSS feeds (tech blogs), ArXiv (for AI/ML users), Stack Overflow trending tags, official release notes.
AI Curation	Send aggregated raw content to LLM (OpenAI GPT-4o / Gemini) with structured prompt. LLM must: (1) Rank by relevance to user’s stack, (2) Deduplicate similar articles, (3) Categorize into sections, (4) Generate 2-3 sentence summaries per item, (5) Score difficulty level.
Sections to Generate	What’s Hot This Week (top 5 trending), New Releases & Updates, Deep Dive (1 long-form recommendation), Quick Tips (3-5 actionable tips), Weekly Learning Path (ordered resources), Try This (hands-on exercise idea)
Caching	Store generated content in Redis with 7-day TTL. Serve from cache for subsequent requests within the week.

2.3 Newsletter View (Mobile)
Feature	Details
Infographic Cards	Each section rendered as a visually distinct card with icons, color coding, progress indicators, and micro-animations. NOT plain text lists.
Swipeable Sections	Horizontal swipe between newsletter sections (What’s Hot → Deep Dive → Tips → Learning Path)
Source Links	Tap any item to open the original article in an in-app browser (Custom Tabs on Android / SFSafariViewController on iOS)
Bookmark / Save	Save individual items for later reading
Share	Share entire newsletter or individual cards as image/PDF via native share sheet
Archive	Access all past weekly newsletters in a scrollable timeline

2.4 Learning Plan
Feature	Details
Weekly Learning Path	AI-generated ordered learning sequence: Read articles → Watch video → Complete exercise
Progress Tracking	Checkbox-style completion tracking per item. Persist progress across sessions.
Streak Counter	Consecutive weeks of completing the learning plan (gamification)
Cumulative Dashboard	Monthly/quarterly view showing topics covered, time invested, skills leveled up
Adaptive Difficulty	If user consistently completes Advanced content, auto-adjust next week’s plan upward

2.5 Settings & Preferences
Feature	Details
Dark/Light/System Theme	Follow system preference by default, allow manual override
Delivery Day	Choose which day the weekly newsletter is generated
Content Density	Compact (5 items) / Standard (10 items) / Detailed (15+ items)
Language	English (v1). Architect for i18n from day one.
Data & Privacy	Export data, delete account, privacy policy display

2.6 Push Notifications
Feature	Details
Weekly Delivery	"Your weekly TechPulse is ready!" — sent when newsletter generation completes
Streak Reminder	Mid-week nudge if learning plan not started: "Don’t break your 4-week streak!"
Trending Alert (v2)	Breaking tech news relevant to user’s stack
 
3. Technical Architecture
3.1 Tech Stack Summary
Layer	Technology
Mobile Framework	Kotlin Multiplatform + Compose Multiplatform
Mobile Language	Kotlin
Backend	Kotlin + Spring Boot (or Java + Spring Boot)
API	RESTful (JSON over HTTPS)
Primary Database	PostgreSQL
Local Database	SQLDelight (cross-platform)
Caching	Redis
AI/LLM	OpenAI API (GPT-4o) or Google Gemini API
Push Notifications	Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)
Cloud	GCP or Azure
CI/CD	GitHub Actions + Fastlane (iOS) + Gradle (Android)
Analytics	Firebase Analytics
Crash Reporting	Firebase Crashlytics

3.2 Project Structure (Clean Architecture)
Follow multi-module clean architecture as per KMP best practices:
project-root/
├── core/
│   ├── network/              # Ktor client, API service interfaces
│   ├── database/             # SQLDelight schemas, DAOs
│   ├── common/               # Shared utilities, extensions, constants
│   ├── designsystem/         # Theme, colors, typography, reusable components
├── features/
│   ├── onboarding/
│   │   ├── domain/           # Use cases: SelectTechStack, SetPreferences
│   │   ├── data/             # Repository implementations
│   │   ├── presentation/     # Compose screens + ViewModels
│   ├── newsletter/
│   │   ├── domain/           # Use cases: GetWeeklyNewsletter, BookmarkItem
│   │   ├── data/             # Repository, API models, mappers
│   │   ├── presentation/     # Infographic cards, swipeable views
│   ├── learningplan/
│   │   ├── domain/           # Use cases: GetLearningPlan, TrackProgress
│   │   ├── data/
│   │   ├── presentation/
│   ├── profile/
│   ├── settings/
├── composeApp/               # App module: navigation, DI, theme
│   ├── src/commonMain/
│   ├── src/androidMain/
│   ├── src/iosMain/
├── androidApp/               # Android entry point
├── iosApp/                   # iOS entry point (Xcode project)

3.3 Key API Endpoints
Method	Endpoint	Description
POST	/api/v1/auth/register	User registration
POST	/api/v1/auth/login	Login, returns JWT
PUT	/api/v1/user/techstack	Update selected technologies
GET	/api/v1/newsletter/weekly	Get current week’s newsletter
GET	/api/v1/newsletter/archive?page=1	Paginated past newsletters
GET	/api/v1/learning-plan/current	Current week’s learning plan
PUT	/api/v1/learning-plan/progress	Update item completion status
POST	/api/v1/newsletter/items/{id}/bookmark	Bookmark an item
GET	/api/v1/user/stats	Streak, topics covered, progress

